<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ua Conchobair dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as O'Conor dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ua Conchobair, later O'Conor, were a dynasty of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-briuin">Uí Briúin</a> who ruled the kingdom of Connacht from the 11th century. Two of its kings, Toirdelbach and his son Ruaidrí, claimed the high kingship of Ireland in the 12th century. After the Anglo-Norman grant of Connacht in 1227 their power shrank to Roscommon, and in 1384 the family split into the O'Conor Don and O'Conor Roe lines.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ua-conchobair-dynasty.jpg" alt="Ua Conchobair dynasty" width="320" height="373" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: self-created · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:O%27Conor.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
